        ecrm:P126_employed      "depressed"@en , "600-756 knots per sq. in (9,024-11,544 per sq. dm).\nWARP: yellow silk"@en , "(2) silver strip, Z-twisted around a white silk core"@en , "192 - 208 warp threads per dm (48 - 54 per in)\nWEFT: Foundation weft: yellow silk"@en , "9024 -11544 knots per sq.dm (600 - 756 knots per sq. in).\nSIDE FINISH: one cord oversewn with dark red silk.\nEND FINISH: Lower: part missing but there are the remains of a tapestry-woven band with an inscription in black and silver thread.  Upper: cut."@en , "14 colours: dark red, light red, dark orange, yellow, dark green, green, light green, very light green, dark blue, blue, very light blue, dark brown, brown, white"@en , "asymmetrical knot open to the left"@en , "Hand-knotted wool pile, on silk warp and weft, with areas brocaded with metal thread"@en , "asymmetrical knot, open to the left"@en , "3 shoots after each row of knots"@en , "94 - 111 knots per dm (25 - 28 knots per in). Pattern weft: (1) silver strip, Z-twisted around a yellow silk core"@en , "brocaded over 3 warp threads.\nPILE: wool"@en , "Z2S"@en ;
